{{Quote|People don't look down to where they should. They don't look down, they don't look past the rust. Not us though, eh? Eyes open, possibilities everywhere.|Clem Andor|<ref name="Rix Road">{{Andor|Rix Road (episode)}}</ref>}}
'''Clem Andor''' was a [[Gender|male]] [[human]] mechanic and salvager from the [[planet]] [[Ferrix]].<ref name="Clem DB" /> Prior to the outbreak of the [[Clone Wars]],<ref name="Andor Trivia1">{{SW|url=andor-s1-e3-trivia-gallery|text="Reckoning" Trivia Gallery &#124; Andor}} {{C|Slide 1}}</ref> he [[Exploratory mission to investigate a downed craft|accompanied]] his [[Marriage|wife]] [[Maarva Carassi Andor|Maarva]] on the planet [[Kenari]], where the pair found and adopted [[Cassian Jeron Andor]].<ref name="Reckoning" />

==Biography==
===Early life===
Clem Andor was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] who was [[Reproduction|born]]<ref name="Rix Road" /> around [[81 BBY]]<ref name="Date" /> and hailed from the [[planet]] [[Ferrix]]<ref name="Clem DB" /> which was located in the [[Free Trade sector]].<ref name="Kassa">{{Andor|Kassa (episode)}}</ref> At some point, Clem married [[Maarva Carassi Andor|Maarva]], and the two worked as scavengers, traversing the galaxy to bring back unclaimed technology to their homeworld.<ref name="Clem DB" />

===Scavenging on Kenari===
[[File:Maarva-Clem-Bee-Reckoning.png|thumb|left|250px|Clem and Maarva scavenged on Kenari with their droid B2EMO.]]
Around [[23 BBY]],<ref name="24BBY">''[[Star Wars: Dawn of Rebellion: The Visual Guide]]'' establishes that [[Cassian Jeron Andor]] was twenty-seven [[Standard year|years]] old during the events of [[Andor Season 1|''Andor'' Season 1]], the events of which are dated to [[5 BBY]] by that same book. {{Databank|cassian-andor|Cassian Andor}} establishes that Andor was nine years old when he left [[Kenari]], with {{SW|url=series/andor/andor-season-1-episode-3-episode-guide|text="Reckoning" Episode Guide &#124; Andor}} establishing that this occurred before the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] had formed. ''[[Rise of the Separatists]]'' and ''[[The Star Wars Book]]'' establish that the [[Raxus Address|formation the CIS]] occurred two [[Standard year|years]] before the [[First Battle of Geonosis]], which ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' and other sources date to take place in [[22 BBY]]. For all this information to be true, Cassian Andor had to have been born in [[33 BBY]], with his departure taking place after his birthday, but before the Raxus Address in [[24 BBY]], and the events of ''Andor'' taking place before his birthday in [[5 BBY]].</ref> Clem, his wife Maarva and their droid [[B2EMO]] embarked on a [[Exploratory mission to investigate a downed craft|mission to salvage wrecked technology and equipment]] from a crashed [[Galactic Republic|Republic]] [[starship]] on the [[planet]] of [[Kenari]]. Amongst the wreckage, Clem and Maarva found Cassian, a young Kenari boy, that had been exploring the wreckage. Though Clem admired the boy's spirit, he was anxious to leave as a separate Republic vessel was approaching. In order to save him, Maarva stunned Cassian and removed him from the wreckage. Returning to Ferrix, Clem and Maarva adopted the boy and raised him as their own.<ref name="Reckoning" />

===Cassian's father===
{{Quote|The man that sees everything is more blessed than cursed.|Clem Andor to his son, Cassian|<ref name="Rix Road" />}}
Clem, Maarva, and Cassian were living in a [[Andor household|household]] in a small town on the planet of [[Ferrix]]. Clem showed his adopted son Cassian how to clean a small type of engine part using an acid bath. He taught the boy the value of looking past the rust of old parts to see the possibilities beneath.<ref name="Rix Road" />

===Protests on Ferrix===
[[File:ClemAndor-Platinum2023.png|thumb|right|180px|Clem was falsely accused of rioting against the Empire.]]
{{Quote|Take me up Rix Road and hang me in the square. Wouldn't be the first time, would it? Isn't that where they hung your father?|[[Luthen Rael]], to Cassian Jeron Andor|<ref name="Reckoning" />}}
In 19 BBY, within the first year of the [[Galactic Empire]]'s rule,<ref name="Dawn of Rebellion date" /> Clem and Cassian were present in the town's square when a large contingent of [[Clone trooper|clone stormtroopers]] and their [[officer]] were marching through. The town's people, upset with the newly-fledged Empire's presence, begun a [[Rix Road Protest|protest]], pelting stones at the passing troopers and demanded for the return of the former Republic and for Ferrix's liberation. Clem unsuccessfully attempted to calm the protestors, citing that they were making the situation worse. In response, the Imperial officer ordered his troopers to raise their weapons against the town's populace. Accused of having taken part in the protest, Clem was subsequently [[Hanging|hanged]] in the town's square at [[Rix Road]].<ref name="Announcement">{{Andor|Announcement}}</ref>

Later, with his father's corpse still hanging, Cassian entered the town's square with his blow gun from Kenari and charged a group of clone stormtroopers intending to kill them, but was apprehended and arrested.<ref name="Announcement" />

At some point later, Clem's body was cremated,<ref name="Rix Road" /> and his ashes mixed with mortar and dust to form his [[funerary stone]],<ref name="DoF">{{Andor|Daughter of Ferrix}}</ref> on which was inscribed his name, date of birth, and date of death. His brick was placed in a wall on a street of the [[Gavalox Communications]] center.<ref name="Rix Road" />

===Legacy===
{{Quote|Think of a name for yourself.''"<br />"''Clem.''"<br />"''For the next five days, you'll be Clem.|Luthen Rael and Cassian Jeron Andor|<ref name="Reckoning" />}}
[[File:Rip_clem_andor.png|thumb|left|250px|Clem Andor's stone]]
After the [[Ambush on Ferrix]], Cassian chose his adoptive father's name as a false identity when undergoing a [[Aldhani heist|mission]] for [[Luthen Rael]].<ref name="Aldhani">{{Andor|Aldhani (episode)}}</ref> Later, when he returned to Ferrix for his mother's [[funeral]] after escaping the [[Narkina 5 Imperial Prison Complex|prison]] on [[Narkina 5]], he visited Clem's [[funerary stone]] and reminisced of their time together.<ref name="Rix Road" />

==Equipment==
[[File:AndorMW20BryarPistol-Reckoning.jpg|thumb|right|150px|Clem's blaster which his adoptive son later used after his death.]]
Around the time of the [[Republic Era]], Clem wielded<ref name="Reckoning" /> an [[MW-20 Bryar pistol]],<ref name="Andor Trivia2">{{SW|url=andor-s1-e3-trivia-gallery|text="Reckoning" Trivia Gallery &#124; Andor}} {{C|Slide 4}}</ref> which was wielded by his adopted son years later. Additionally, he utilized a [[breath mask]] while scavenging on [[Kenari]]. He [[Pilot|co-piloted]] the [[Andor family hauler|hauler]] he and Maarva owned.<ref name="Reckoning" />

==Behind the scenes==
Clem Andor first appeared in "[[Reckoning (episode)|Reckoning]]," the third episode of the television series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'', portrayed by [[Gary Beadle]].<ref name="Reckoning" /> The [[2023 Topps Star Wars|2023 ''Topps Star Wars'']] card set mistakenly lists his homeworlds as [[Kenari]] and [[Aldhani]],<ref name="2023 Topps">{{Topps|set=2023 Topps Star Wars|cardname=Clem Andor|link=https://www.tcdb.com/ViewCard.cfm/sid/370777/cid/22170367/2023-Topps-Star-Wars-37-Clem-Andor}}</ref> even though the [[Databank (2014-)|Databank]] previously established it as [[Ferrix]].<ref name="Clem DB" />

If the [[Coruscant reckoning calendar]] and [['ABY-BBY' dating system]] are one-to-one, then the 7959 C.R.C. death dating found on Andor's funerary stone narrows his death date down to [[18 BBY]].<ref name="Old Death Date">{{SW|url=andor-s1-e12-trivia-gallery|text="Rix Road" Trivia Gallery &#124; Andor}} {{C|Slide 2}} dates Clem Andor's [[death]] to 7959 [[Coruscant reckoning calendar|C.R.C.]] ''[[Star Wars: Scum and Villainy: Case Files on the Galaxy's Most Notorious]]'' dates [[Plot to assassinate Senator Amidala|assassination attempt]] on [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]] on [[Coruscant]] to 7955 C.R.C., which ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates to [[22 BBY]], therefore it can be concluded that 7959 C.R.C. is equivalent to [[18 BBY]].</ref> However, the reference book ''[[Star Wars: Dawn of Rebellion: The Visual Guide]]'' later established Andor's death to occur in 19 BBY through its dating of his son's arrest.<ref name="Dawn of Rebellion date" /> As the C.R.C and BBY calendars would have different start dates,<ref name="Calendar Different">{{Bluesky|infinata.bsky.social|post/3ku4i3fxkbq2b|[[Pablo Hidalgo]]|date=2024-06-04|quote=They would all have different start dates, as two are event-based and one is an arbitary calendar. {{C|In response to: "Hi Pabro. I purchased "Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary" yesterday and have enjoyed reading it. Does the fact that the consolation to Rosal [''sic''] is placed at 36 BSI mean that BSI/ASI and BBY/ABY are not just 34 years apart, but have different "Januarys"? Also could this also be said about the C.R.C.?"}}|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/4wbBM}}</ref> this article assumes this is not a contradiction, but simply a difference between two calendars.

